# Project Agent Skills

- Cursor discovers **Agent Skills** from **`.cursor/skills/*/`** and **`.agents/skills/*/`** (each skill is a folder with `SKILL.md`; see [Cursor Skills](https://cursor.com/docs/context/skills)).
- This repo mirrors the same skills under **`.agents/skills/`** (symlinks → `.cursor/skills/`) so both discovery paths resolve.
- When the user’s task matches a skill’s **description** (e.g. `/keys/use-cases`, marketing flow diagrams, product-proof pages), **read that skill’s `SKILL.md` first** before large edits—do not rely on memory alone.
- **Also read the matching skill first** for: **suite or module landings** (`/`, `/keys`, `/testing`, `/graph`), **`/integrations`**, **integration catalog or ecosystem strips**, **third-party logos** (`restormel-suite-integrations-marketing`, `restormel-third-party-brand-marks`, `restormel-integration-docs-hub`).
- For **large cross-route marketing or IA refactors**, prefer the **Task tool** (e.g. `explore`) to inventory affected routes before editing; keep edits narrow per [.cursor/rules/06-credit-efficiency.mdc](./06-credit-efficiency.mdc).
- New project skills: add under **`.cursor/skills/<kebab-name>/SKILL.md`**, set frontmatter **`name`** to match the folder name exactly, then add a matching symlink under **`.agents/skills/`**.
